        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Puneet Mishra</h1>
        <p class="deck">
          I write about the parts of systems work that don't fit in a commit message.
        </p>

        <p>
          Most of what shows up here comes out of building high-throughput ingest
          services in Rust — pipelines that decode binary protocol frames and load
          them into PostgreSQL, at rates where every allocation and every syscall
          starts to matter.
        </p>

        <p>
          The posts describe <strong>techniques</strong>, not products. Where a
          technique came out of professional work, the engineering is the subject
          and the business context is left out entirely. Every figure and every
          benchmark on this site is reproduced on synthetic data generated for
          that purpose, so the numbers are mine to publish.
        </p>

        <p class="note"><b>Protocols</b>DLMS/COSEM appears throughout. It is a published open standard — IEC 62056 — so nothing about parsing it is anyone's secret.</p>

        <p>
          Find me on <a href="https://github.com/0xpun337">GitHub</a>, or subscribe
          via <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
